No, that can't happen. Monster speeds are governed by mcalcmove() in
mon.c, which uses mon->data->mmove. The entire mon->data structure is
generated afresh by newcham() in mon.c.

You can easily confirm this by using #monpolycontrol in wizard mode to
turn a speed-36 air elemental into a speed-3 wumpus. The wumpus does not
zoom across the room and pummel you.

Many monster speeds are quite seriously crazy.
